## Verification Standard

When reviewing work, apply the three-tier standard:

| Tier | Evidence |
|------|----------|
| DONE | Runtime artifact (API response, DB query, screenshot) |
| VERIFIED | AC line-by-line with code citations |
| AUDITED | File exists, function names match |

Report tiers separately. Never upgrade a tier without evidence.

## Red Lines

- No `as any` on database operations without migration reference
- No silent error swallowing in financial operations
- No `{ data }` without `{ error }` on database queries
- No self-grading — Stark cannot verify their own work
- No hand-rolled auth lookups — use the centralized helper

